    {
      "id": "claim_c912d93b69fb4e54b1461ab0ecbf7392",
      "statement": "requireAuth performs no validation of `sub`, so the two requirements docs/API.md places on it are enforced only indirectly by Postgres: `sub` must be a UUID (user_armies.user_id and user_unit_media.user_id are @db.Uuid columns) and a matching user_profiles row must already exist via the ON DELETE CASCADE foreign key, provisioned directly in the database until a signup endpoint lands - no code path in the repo creates user_profiles rows. A non-UUID or unprovisioned `sub` therefore fails inside Postgres and surfaces as HTTP 500 DB_ERROR rather than a client error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/middleware/auth.ts#L32-L42",
