    {
      "id": "claim_5eba2cc38f1040eaba5edeb9c13998d6",
      "statement": "The web client obtains its bearer token from a legacy Supabase session (getAuthToken -> supabase.auth.getSession -> access_token), which is signed by the Supabase project's secret rather than the instance's JWT_SECRET, so requireAuth rejects it with 401 TOKEN_INVALID. No roster function special-cases 401: each wraps apiFetch in try/catch and falls back to localStorage persistence, making roster mutations appear successful in the UI while nothing is written to Postgres.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/src/lib/api.ts#L243-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aeb4db800b028d221c3ac4455dd18c22b4a2dd3d6cbb237230902b976531cb80:"
