    {
      "id": "claim_e6b1b80c06d5405e9b030d85324e49dd",
      "statement": "Because the production composition's credential fallbacks (JWT_SECRET=please-change-me, postgres/postgrespassword) are public in the repository, docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §2 states that anyone who can read the repo can mint valid auth tokens against a server still using them; the zero-config boot is intentional for CI/test environments, which makes overriding JWT_SECRET mandatory for anything reachable beyond localhost and leaves no tooling that verifies the operator did so.",
